  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday night through next Thursday)\nIssued at 148 PM CDT Thu May 21 2026\n\nRain chances will continue through a good portion of the extended \nperiod, along with cooler than normal temperatures. Several weak \ndisturbances in southwest flow aloft will traverse the area for \nthe start of the weekend. In addition, a weak cold front will \nenter northwest Texas early Saturday and gradually work south \nacross the area into Saturday night. The front, coupled with \nthe upper level disturbances, will result in medium to high rain \nchances (40-80%) Saturday into Saturday night. The threat for \nsevere weather will be low however, due to weaker flow aloft. \nModels continue to show a weak cutoff low developing over east \nTexas Sunday into Monday, with ridging aloft to the west of this \nfeature over west Texas. This pattern will keep most of the \nprecipitation east of the area, although low rain chances will \npersist across southeast portions of the forecast area during\nthe afternoon hours. \n\nLow to medium chances return again next Tuesday through Thursday,\nas another trough to the west begins to affect the region.",
